# Observe Agent Turns

This Livebook attaches a telemetry handler to the terminal event for one Agent
Turn. The handler sends the event to this notebook process.

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Define an Agent

```elixir
defmodule ObserveGuide.Counter do
  use Jido.Agent, name: "observe_guide_counter"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{count: Zoi.integer() |> Zoi.default(0)})
  end

  routes do
    signal_source "/guides/observe"

    route "counter.add" do
      action %{amount: amount},
        name: "observe_guide_add",
        schema: Zoi.object(%{amount: Zoi.integer()}),
        context: context do
        {:ok, %{context.agent_state | count: context.agent_state.count + amount}}
      end

      define :add, args: [:amount]
    end
  end
end

defmodule ObserveGuide.Forwarder do
  def handle(event, measurements, metadata, receiver) do
    send(receiver, {:agent_turn, event, measurements, metadata})
  end
end
```

## Attach a handler

Telemetry handlers run in the process that emits the event. Keep the handler
small and send work to another process.

```elixir
observer = self()
handler_id = "observe-guide-#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}"

:ok =
  :telemetry.attach(
    handler_id,
    [:jido, :agent, :turn, :settled],
    &ObserveGuide.Forwarder.handle/4,
    observer
  )
```

## Run one Turn

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()

{:ok, counter} =
  Jido.start_agent(
    Jido.default_instance(),
    ObserveGuide.Counter,
    id: "observed-counter"
  )

{:ok, committed} = ObserveGuide.Counter.add(counter, 2)
committed.state
```

The settled event reports the final outcome after Directive handling. A Turn
can commit and then fail during post-commit work, so inspect both `:status` and
`:committed?`.

```elixir
event =
  receive do
    {:agent_turn, name, measurements, metadata} ->
      %{name: name, measurements: measurements, metadata: metadata}
  after
    5_000 ->
      raise "no Agent Turn event arrived"
  end

%{
  status: event.metadata.status,
  committed?: event.metadata.committed?,
  signal_type: event.metadata.signal_type,
  state_version_after: event.measurements.state_version_after
}
```

Metadata is bounded. It includes stable identity, Signal, Turn, trace, status,
and stage fields. It excludes Agent state, Signal payloads, process handles,
caller context, and raw error details.

## Detach and stop

```elixir
:ok = :telemetry.detach(handler_id)
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(Jido.default_instance(), counter)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

Read [Telemetry, Tracing, and Logs](telemetry-tracing-and-logs.html) before you
connect a production exporter.
